I could not run the exact worst-case calculation for this maze, so this controller is a heuristic built from the sensors, not a verified optimum. It should be checked against the 0.56 requirement before relying on it.

The idea is that at each crossing Pac-Man should avoid stepping toward either ghost. The ghosts start at (3,4), right next to Pac-Man's route, and turn toward him, so the strictest rule comes first. Rules then relax in stages, and the last `any` rules allow the directions that are merely not closer to a ghost. Only if every direction is unsafe does the catch-all send him right. Because the conditions use only sensors and never step counts or cell coordinates, the same list applies unchanged to games of any length.

{"rules": [
{"condition": "!wall & !nearer_g0 & !nearer_g1 & !closer_g0 & !closer_g1", "action": "any"},
{"condition": "!closer_g0 & !closer_g1 & !wall", "action": "any"},
{"condition": "!closer_g0 & !closer_g1", "action": "any"},
{"condition": "!nearer_g0 & !nearer_g1", "action": "any"},
{"condition": "true", "action": "right"}
]}
